{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/575811-dragon-blooded-design-and-charm-space-for-3e","id":575811,"title":"Dragon-Blooded design and charm space for 3E","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-01T17:49:31-07:00","id":575811,"title":"Dragon-Blooded design and charm space for 3E","content":"So for some time now I've been looking over the existing 2E and 2.5E Dragon-Blooded charm set and thinking of the possibility of moving it out of an ability bound system. Ever since I first had the chance to look at Infernals and how they work in 2E, both in structure and on a mechanical power level, I thought to myself 'This is exactly where I'd want Dragon-Blooded to be.' I think giving the Dragon-Blooded 6 charm cascades(one for each element and one for general effects that could suit any elemental flavor such as Elemental Bolt) better reinforces the idea that Aspect does not dictate role (like Castes do). It also frees Dragon-Blooded from being sold short as 'could have been Celestial's and allowing them to be more varied and interesting in how they approach a given situation.<br /> <br /> So my questions are as follows:<br /> <br /> To the developers: Will we see any changes to the Dragon-Blooded in regards to the abilities being tied to only one of the elements?<br /> <br /> To the community: Are there any other Dragon-Blooded fans interested in this sort of design space? Perhaps enough to join a combined homebrew effort?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2394-grifnir","name":"Grifnir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T18:07:49-07:00","id":575845,"title":"","content":"Last I heard, Dragon-Blooded are still going to be ability-based, but there will be a lot more flexibility in what element is associated with what ability. Shooting wind blades from your sword (a fire ability) was a cited example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T18:08:32-07:00","id":575847,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d be lying if I said I hadn\u2019t had similar thoughts myself on multiple occasions.<br /> <br /> I think there should also be room for a potential 7<sup>th</sup> cascade of elementless charms. The need to shoehorn every DB charm into having an appropriately elemental effect always bothered me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3355-not-a-platypus","name":"Not a Platypus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T18:14:29-07:00","id":575852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifnir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/575811-dragon-blooded-design-and-charm-space-for-3e#post575811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the developers: Will we see any changes to the Dragon-Blooded in regards to the abilities being tied to only one of the elements?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless something drastic has changed, the Dragon-Blooded set is still Ability-based. It sounded like a given Ability will still be mostly associated with its respective elemental Aspect, but that other elements may feature as well. I... am having trouble finding a particular quote on that last bit, but am convinced I've read it; possibly in the DB backer preview PDF. They have also suggested there may be more fluid elemental control accessible through certain (possibly DB-only) martial arts.<br /> <br /> Some quotes I could find from <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Charms#Dragon-Blooded_Charms\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalts#Dragon-Blooded\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EX3 What We Know Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Q: (nicodemus144)</b><br /> Exalted 3rd Dragon-Blooded: can you speak to whether or not players will be able to evoke Avatar: TLA with the system as written?<br /> <br /> <b>A: (John M\u00f8rke)</b><br /> Avatar evokes Dragon-Blooded. Just throwin' that out there. That said, I plan to introduce some more iconic elemental Charms to various abilities, and probably a new series of five (tentatively) DB-only martial arts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Q: (Arteliex)</b><br /> Will the Dragon-Blooded still have Elemental Bolt, and be much the same as previous editions (Elemental Bolt then upgrade to Elemental Burst)? I'm wondering if it'll still be there, or if instead, it will change to a more fluid form of Element Control.<br /> <br /> <b>A: (John M\u00f8rke)</b><br /> Elemental Bolt? Yes. Elemental Burst? We'll see. Fluid control: Through new martial arts styles, probably.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>(John M\u00f8rke)</b><br /> The whole EX3 team is excited to talk about our plans for Dragon-Blooded, but we have a bit of push left to do on the corebook. I will say this: there will be martial arts and Evocations that let Dragon-Blooded have more flashy elemental powers. We are also spicing up and broadening their Charm set. But do not expect them to have a basic element-bending power or 2e Infernal style designs, because that misses the point of the humanity present in the Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To the community: Are there any other Dragon-Blooded fans interested in this sort of design space? Perhaps enough to join a combined homebrew effort? </div> </div> </div>I expect so. I don't have the sort of time, interest or skill to participate, but I'd be interested to see the fruits of such a project after the DB book is out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T19:47:43-07:00","id":575945,"title":"","content":"They're actually going the opposite direction and making Infernals Ability-based. Putting Infernal charms into a small number of very large charm-trees apparently caused mechanical problems.<br /> <br /> They are, apparently, changing how Caste Abilities work for Solars. I think what we last read was that each Solar Caste has 8 potential Caste Abilities, and you pick 5 of those at character creation.<br /> <br /> I <b><i>hope</i></b> that Dragon-Blooded Abilities work similar, with most or all Abilities having more than one potential elemental association.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 07-01-2015, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T21:18:07-07:00","id":576009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/575811-dragon-blooded-design-and-charm-space-for-3e?p=575945#post575945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're actually going the opposite direction and making Infernals Ability-based. Putting Infernal charms into a small number of very large charm-trees apparently caused mechanical problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually thought Infernals sat in a realm comparable to Lunars in 2E in many ways. The mechanical problems of their broad charm structure was one of them, in addition to the issue of making Infernals into micro-Yozi. As a result, I have no complaints with ability based Infernals.<br /> <br /> For Dragon-Blooded in particular, however, my aversion to ability based charm trees is due to several charms having multiple elemental options but still having surcharges based on the ability's aspect instead of the charm's. If out of aspect surcharges either go away (which would eliminate a lot of bean counting that only serves as a reminder of weakness), or become mitigated by say, a keyword for allowing a malleable charm aspect, it would go a long way toward dismissing my reservations. As it stands now though, having a Fire Elemental Bolt invoking a elemental surcharge to a Fire aspect for not being an Air Aspect, just seems silly to me.<br /> <br /> If the writers allow some wiggle room in charm/ability aspect I'll be happy. More importantly though, I would be overjoyed if we could remove all blanket failure conditions from their charm space. It would be a shame to let them go another edition defined by their weakness instead of their uniqueness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2394-grifnir","name":"Grifnir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T21:49:25-07:00","id":576026,"title":"","content":"They'll be getting rid of surcharges. They know how much the community as a whole hated those things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T00:16:57-07:00","id":576130,"title":"","content":"I'm going to reiterate my liking of Ability Charms for giving a firm and straightforward grasp of what kinds of narratives you actually pursue with the Charms. I get a much stronger idea of what to do with a Water Aspect with Bureaucracy than I do a lot of ideas for Water Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T01:02:46-07:00","id":576172,"title":"","content":"At the same time though, I have lots of ideas for Melee Charms that revolve around the element of Water, and quite a few Craft ideas based around the idea of Wood. It was always rather unfortunate that that those weren't really possible in the previous editions.<br /> <br /> I am hoping that there will be a lot more freedom in 3rd edition to introduce Charms (maybe even entire Charm trees) based an Element into an Ability associated with a different Element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T01:16:41-07:00","id":576209,"title":"","content":"No I'm perfectly all right with things like Melee being given some inroads for &quot;adaptable and inscrutable&quot; and &quot;nurturing and toxic&quot; emotional and intellectual profiles, and even the &quot;resembles water and wood stuff&quot;. Although there are some things where the &quot;resembles the element&quot; part feels overt enough that I wouldn't think there was very much outside of the Aspect association (mostly Sail). Either way, just... stuff you can readily build characters with methods and aspirations out of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T02:36:02-07:00","id":576246,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of expanding each aspect's set of abilities and then asking you to pick some of those, and then you can get some free picks of any abilities to round them out.<br /> <br /> Means that aspect feels a little less restrictive and a little more helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T02:51:39-07:00","id":576252,"title":"","content":"Also good on that point if it carries over - less &quot;any fire aspect who doesn't focus on melee is wasting one of their extremely limited abilities&quot;. Sure, I'll swap melee for performance and take martial arts and be a tango dancer with brutally powerful kicks, without having to feel that's a water concept just because of caste abilities rather than caste flavor!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T16:12:10-07:00","id":576873,"title":"","content":"Part of my love for Dragonblooded comes from the idea that they have elemental kung fu in *every* Ability.<br /> <br /> Which is why I like them having Ability based Charms, because that structure guarantees them that they get to have what is to mortal medicine as fire kung fu is to simple brawling. No other Charm structure really guarantees that in the same way, or focuses them towards this, or makes it so clear that they *are* this. They are the guys who know in their soul the essence of flame, rock, sea, wind, creeping branch and choking vine, the ones in who this essence flows and they use it to perform feats of superhuman ability.<br /> <br /> (Note the Immaculate Martial Arts fit into this as Dragonbloodedness squared - they're extra potent ultra concentrated essence of elemental kung fu, what the Dragonblooded whose very nature is elemental kung fu in everything would see as elemental kung fu.)<br /> <br /> (Another note - I have probably overused the words elemental kung fu here and thus alienated some from the concept ;( ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T02:31:36-07:00","id":577175,"title":"","content":"I support the idea of making the Charms more varied and easier to use, but I personally like the Aspect Abilities as they're currently spread out. Even if a particular character is oriented towards Martial Arts (which is facilitated by Favoured Abilities), I would still be inclined to play out their passionate, energetic warrior stuff in the manner implied by things like Melee and Presence and Socialize being Aspect Abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T03:01:35-07:00","id":577186,"title":"","content":"I definitely feel that each Aspect should have abilities related to it's nature. But I think that, as with all game design, it's all very well being clever with what your mechanics say about something, but they key aim for all gameplay is obviously to facilitate the game and give players options while retaining the focus on the milieu. So I'd expand each Aspect to cover a slightly broader base of abilities (what they are now, plus two or three more), then give picks, then give free picks. Because then you are giving people elemental flavour and also options, which seems like the best course. If that causes overlaps between the Aspects, that's not necessarily a bad thing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T16:07:53-07:00","id":577904,"title":"","content":"If my memory serves me right, of the dB sail napkin spoiler, every ability will be elemental neutral to a point then branch out so that specific elemental themes are met. With a final set of 2 to 4 charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T10:22:58-07:00","id":578920,"title":"","content":"My first draft of the Dragon-Blooded Charmset didn't work out, for various reasons, which invalidates some of the inferences that may have been drawn from the spoilers. But yeah, I am almost 100% certain they will remain Ability-based, with elemental aspects threaded through them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T05:20:16-07:00","id":579731,"title":"","content":"Can you tell us if the intention still is to allow multiple elemental expressions of the same ability? It's important for different ideas I have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T19:22:37-07:00","id":580450,"title":"","content":"The one thing I hope is that they get rid of the mote surcharge for out-of-aspect charms. I've always found that one thing infuriating for some reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/692-herrtenko","name":"HerrTenko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T21:10:47-07:00","id":580517,"title":"","content":"It makes your character very restricted combat-wise: using out-of-aspect combat abilities (like a fire aspect who punches people with his flaming fists, a wood aspect who fights with a wooden staff, or an Earth aspect who tries to fight in any way at all) is extremely sub-optimal. Although for abilities like Survival, Craft, Occult or Linguistics, it doesn't matter too much.<br /> So it encouraged you to play Fire Aspects (for melee and dodge) or Water Aspects (for martial arts) and discouraged you from playing an Earth Aspect.<br /> It also annoyed me because I was sure the other players always forgot about it.<br /> Plus, the way it was once per action (or tick? I don't remember) rather than once per charm-use, meant you couldn't just include it on the cost of charms when you wrote them down on your sheet (for example, you couldn't just say a 3rd excellency was 4m instead of 3m, because if you used it to defend against a flurry, it would be 4m for the first attack and 3m for the others) so you always had to remember, and as I said, I think people often forgot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T22:17:03-07:00","id":580546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifnir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/575811-dragon-blooded-design-and-charm-space-for-3e#post575811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for some time now I've been looking over the existing 2E and 2.5E Dragon-Blooded charm set and thinking of the possibility of moving it out of an ability bound system. Ever since I first had the chance to look at Infernals and how they work in 2E, both in structure and on a mechanical power level, I thought to myself 'This is exactly where I'd want Dragon-Blooded to be.'</div> </div> </div> </div>I know this wasn't your main point, but DB absolutely should not be on the same mechancal power level as celestials. They out number all celestial exalted ten to one. Making them as powerful both makes the return of the Solars sort of meh and raises the question of why the loss of the Lawgivers was even an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T22:36:31-07:00","id":580555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/575811-dragon-blooded-design-and-charm-space-for-3e?p=580546#post580546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know this wasn't your main point, but DB absolutely should not be on the same mechancal power level as celestials. They out number all celestial exalted ten to one. Making them as powerful both makes the return of the Solars sort of meh and raises the question of why the loss of the Lawgivers was even an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps I should have elaborated further. It's not that I want Dragon-Blooded to be equal to celestials. What I would like ideally is that the overall gap between tiers be much narrower.than it was in 2E (which seems to be the devs goal if I'm understanding things correctly.) The way it stands now mechanically, a single Elder Solar could slaughter a usurpation's worth of Elder Dragon-Blooded with little real threat to his own life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2394-grifnir","name":"Grifnir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T00:08:12-07:00","id":580595,"title":"","content":"3rd edition will be moving back closer to 1st edition where the gap between Celestial and Terrestrial wasn't so big, and there wasn't as much of a gap between Solaroid's and the other Celestial Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T12:17:35-07:00","id":581364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/575811-dragon-blooded-design-and-charm-space-for-3e?p=577186#post577186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'd expand each Aspect to cover a slightly broader base of abilities (what they are now, plus two or three more), then give picks, then give free picks. Because then you are giving people elemental flavour and also options, which seems like the best course. If that causes overlaps between the Aspects, that's not necessarily a bad thing!</div> </div> </div> </div>It would make it possible, for example, to write/convert Firearms/Flamepiece charms for Archery and put them under fire instead of wood.<br /> <br /> What 3 additional abilities would you give to each aspect? For combat charms I'd give Archery to Fire, Brawl/Martial Arts to Earth, and Melee to Wood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T12:37:30-07:00","id":581385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/575811-dragon-blooded-design-and-charm-space-for-3e?p=581364#post581364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would make it possible, for example, to write/convert Firearms/Flamepiece charms for Archery and put them under fire instead of wood.<br /> <br /> What 3 additional abilities would you give to each aspect? For combat charms I'd give Archery to Fire, Brawl/Martial Arts to Earth, and Melee to Wood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno, really. You could argue most Abilities to be elementally connected to most elements.<br /> <br /> What I would do beyond that, though, is reduce the amount of Aspect picks and increase the free picks. So, say, eight Aspect Abilities, select four of them, and then select any four abilities, and there's your core set. Then Aspect is much more forgiving and empowering, and feels like much more a help in chargen than a hindrance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T14:28:56-07:00","id":581543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/575811-dragon-blooded-design-and-charm-space-for-3e?p=581364#post581364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would make it possible, for example, to write/convert Firearms/Flamepiece charms for Archery and put them under fire instead of wood.<br /> <br /> What 3 additional abilities would you give to each aspect? For combat charms I'd give Archery to Fire, Brawl/Martial Arts to Earth, and Melee to Wood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't spread offensive combat Ability picks around at all, except MAYBE giving Earth Brawl as an option or something. I'd do the rest with all defensive combat Abilities and non-combat Abilities. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/575811-dragon-blooded-design-and-charm-space-for-3e?p=581385#post581385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I would do beyond that, though, is reduce the amount of Aspect picks and increase the free picks. So, say, eight Aspect Abilities, select four of them, and then select any four abilities, and there's your core set. Then Aspect is much more forgiving and empowering, and feels like much more a help in chargen than a hindrance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a cool idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T14:42:41-07:00","id":581557,"title":"","content":"I'd consider giving each two core &quot;combat&quot; picks, a couple of useful physical picks (so not attack roll skills but stuff like stealth, athletics, ride etc), a couple of social, couple of knowledge etc<br /> <br /> So, Air have Linguistics, Lore, Occult, Stealth and Thrown. I'd expand that to include, like, Athletics, Archery and Socialise (just purely as examples).<br /> <br /> I'd prossibly also introduce a MtG style wheel too, with two allied and two opposing aspects for each, and then something like an XP break to learn allied charms (but no penalty for opposing and with abilities selected out of aspect at chargen still getting base aspect XP costs), but that's more an off the top of my head idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T15:47:37-07:00","id":581634,"title":"","content":"Functionally, if you keep an &quot;out-of-X&quot; mote surcharge, but don't apply it to any Caste OR Favored, functionally speaking, you can keep the notion of &quot;powers not closely associated to you are more taxing&quot; while functionally closing the One True Build loophole that DBs suffer from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T15:56:31-07:00","id":581641,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't want to penalise any charm options, though, I'd rather just give XP breaks on some stuff to reward playing to a broader elemental theme. I tend towards carrot rather than stick in game design. But that's just a brief thought, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T16:03:36-07:00","id":581648,"title":"","content":"I prefer carrot too. Just throwing the idea out there in case the surcharge sticks around.<br /> <br /> Realistically speaking, people don't tend to take many Charms outside Caste and Favored, and if they do take a couple, they're probably not &quot;core concept&quot; powers but fillers for competency holes. So with those I'm ok bumping the price a little, since the issue will probably be rare to come up. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure how you design XP breaks like you suggest. &quot;Playing to an elemental theme&quot; would seem to be a thing considered on such an individualized basis that it's hard to consider a broad rule for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T16:09:35-07:00","id":581650,"title":"","content":"Yeah that's why I'd probably just chuck it out as an idea.<br /> <br /> I'd really want to just make DBs a bit more flexible when it comes to their Abilities, but I think that increasing the Aspect options and decreasing the amount of Abilities you need to have in Aspect would do that just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T16:12:22-07:00","id":581654,"title":"","content":"I quite liked the concept of Charms having a different effect for each element, but where you could still pay XP to get other element than your Aspect's - as long as it's not a whole Charm cost.<br /> <br /> Speaking about Charm repurchase, I really wish we could have more equivalents of the Alchemicals submodules : repurchase being a whole Charm cost (with no middle ground with the 0XP autoupgrade), makes either Charms too weak or a kitchen sink effect where you stuff effects together to make it worth the cost. It really lacks flexibility. The technology exist, and I see no real reason to keep it specific to Alchemicals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://oi61.tinypic.com/30cn5ug.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> A.K.A. Xelloss33","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/924-xelloss","name":"Xelloss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar924_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T22:01:42-07:00","id":581940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/575811-dragon-blooded-design-and-charm-space-for-3e?p=578920#post578920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first draft of the Dragon-Blooded Charmset didn't work out, for various reasons, which invalidates some of the inferences that may have been drawn from the spoilers. But yeah, I am almost 100% certain they will remain Ability-based, with elemental aspects threaded through them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just realized, what happened to that draft you had? Some of those spoiler charms sounded pretty cool. Might they be added into a book later?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T02:21:28-07:00","id":582058,"title":"","content":"I'm with the OP suggestion in that &quot;Charms not being shackled to Abilities&quot; struck me as a FANTASTIC idea (to the point where I'd rather *Solars* ditched them), but yeah - that is the road not being travelled this edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T03:14:14-07:00","id":582072,"title":"","content":"Abilities are about as much as a shackle as metre is to verse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T07:38:06-07:00","id":582255,"title":"","content":"Edit: oh for charm design! Yeah I like ability charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T11:27:28-07:00","id":582539,"title":"","content":"Overall, after reviewing dev comments, spoilers, and ks preview (and the added confidence in Vance). I'm optimistic we'll see lovingly crafted Dragon-Blooded set in 3E, as opposed to another 1E (or a 1E+excellencies) Dragon-Blooded set. The anticipation is overwhelming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/239